'''Catburger''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that could be unlocked by playing the [[Summer Break Cats Paradise (Event Gacha)|Summer Break Cats Paradise]] Event Gacha. It was added in [[Version 4.2 Update|Version 4.2]]. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 6.4 Update|Version 6.4]] ([[Version 11.1 Update|Version 11.1]] in the Japanese version) increases range. In [[The Battle Cats Unite!]], Catburger was added in [[The Battle Cats Unite!/Patch 1.0.5 Update|Patch 1.0.5]]; however, it is unobtainable without modifying a save file.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 213
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Catburger
|name2 = Cat Royale
|name3 = Value Meal Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Cat Royale''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Value Meal Cat''' when using [[Catfruit]] and XP at level 30.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal Form'''===
Very similar to [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] in terms of usage. Cheap and expendable, it can be summoned en masse to take hits in place of other, more important units. This meatshield role is quite valuable, if not for the wide selection of cats able to perform this role without relevant differences in quality. Catburger, however, can be used in {{4c}} stages, where there is considerably less competition. This is its only use.

==='''Evolved/True Form'''===
Due to the low stats and 10 times the cost, these forms are not recommended as they are considerably worse than any possible alternative in about every way, resulting in them being a bad investment of money. Could still be of use in early-mid [[Empire of Cats]], but, after that, it is best to revert this cat to Normal Form and only use that. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] entirely outclass Catburger, even in True Form.

{{Job|Classification = Meatshield|EvolvedClass = Midranger|UltraClass=}}

